{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/": {
      "title": "Do life-changing work",
      "description": "Do life-changing work | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Do life-changing work Southern New Hampshire University’s innovative, mission-driven work attracts people who want to change the world. From recent graduates to former Fortune 500 leaders, our people have unique backgrounds, experiences and talents. They're what make us shine. No higher ed experience? No problem. In addition to student-facing jobs, our staff includes marketing managers, data analysts, IT specialists and countless others. Whether you’re looking at entry-level jobs or leadership positions, your work has the power to transform lives. Ready to find your team? Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Online Teaching Jobs Student Jobs Roles that fit your goals Maybe you’re looking for something you know you’re great at — a job that’s similar to what you do right now. Or maybe you’re itching for something new and want to steer your career in another direction. No matter what your goals are, there may be a role just for you here at SNHU. Let’s help you find it. View all jobs Our approach to hiring We get it, applying for jobs (especially your dream job) can be… a lot . That's why we've broken it down from the moment you apply to the moment you accept the offer — so you can feel ready to put your best foot forward. Know what to expect Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/online-teaching-jobs/": {
      "title": "Online Teaching Jobs",
      "description": "Online Teaching Jobs | Adjunct Professor Positions | SNHU | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Online Teaching Jobs Adjunct teaching jobs at Southern New Hampshire University give you the unique opportunity to focus on what matters — our students. When you join our team, you can expect to make a difference that is truly life-changing. As an online adjunct instructor, you'll leverage your real-world experiences and insights to add value to predesigned curriculum. You’ll champion our learners, meet them where they’re at and help them overcome barriers. Most of all, when you teach online at SNHU, you'll give students the confidence and support they need to succeed in the classroom and beyond . Remote academics & teaching jobs Play video What's it like to teach online at SNHU? Our online adjunct faculty all have one thing in common — they ’re committed to student success . Check out the video to learn more about our adjunct instructors: who they are, what they do and why their work matters to them. Our people say it best I have gotten so much support from the academic team, the deans that we work with, our team leads, the advisors. It's really been a positive experience overall, but it's working with our learners that I like best. Pamme B. Online Adjunct Instructor Open opportunities Check out the latest roles available in academics and teaching. Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Ethics Save Saved Adjunct Remote See more jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Online Adjunct Faculty FAQs How do I apply for an online adjunct faculty position? Online adjunct faculty positions are available to eligible applicants who reside in and are authorized to work in the United States (with the exception of California). For a full list of qualifications, please reference your specific job posting. Not sure where to start? Take the following steps: Check out our comprehensive list of our academic programs . External Applicants: View our open jobs to apply. When applying, you'll be prompted to sign in to an existing account or create a new account, if needed. After applying, you'll have the ability to sign in to your account at any time to check the status of your application(s). Internal Applicants: Current employees must sign in to their Workday account and navigate to the Employee Jobs Hub to view and apply for positions. What kind of training do you offer for new adjunct faculty? As an adjunct faculty member, you’ll play a critical role in our mission to transform the lives of learners — which is why we offer the support you need to succeed, too. New faculty will be asked to complete an asynchronous 3-week paid online training program. These trainings, delivered in a cohort model, will require active participation throughout each week. Facilitated by dedicated faculty trainers with SNHU experience, the topics covered include: Understanding SNHU's faculty expectations Best practices for teaching online Creating student-centered learning communities Effectively using SNHU academic technologies The course is delivered through our online learning management system: Brightspace. Are there ongoing training and development opportunities for online adjuncts? Yes! SNHU is passionate about promoting continued learning. That’s why we offer online adjunct faculty training and professional development opportunities through COLT (Center for Online Learning and Teaching). COLT is accredited through the IACET (International association for Continuing Education and Training). This means many of COLT’s learning events also award continuing education units (CEUs) upon successful completion. How many classes can I teach at SNHU? In most cases, adjunct instructors may teach 1-2 courses per term with up to 10 course assignments per academic year allowed. What is the process for teaching assignments? When will I know I’ve been assigned? Course assignments are made by our scheduling team, with the guidance of the associate deans. Assignments are made on a term-by-term basis, about 8 weeks prior to the start of the term. Please note that while we’ll work hard to accommodate scheduling requests whenever we can, we’re not always able to guarantee a regular schedule, or teaching assignments every term. What do online classes at SNHU look like? Here’s what to expect from online classes at SNHU: Asynchronous : Students will engage with materials and assignments on their own schedule, while still adhering to course deadlines and requirements. The asynchronous learning setup accommodates diverse schedules and time zones. Courses run 8-10 weeks and include weekly assignments. Class size : Most courses have 25-30 students, promoting interaction and engagement. Some courses, such as writing intensive courses, may have lower course caps. Curriculum : Pre-built courses maintain uniformity in topics, grading and rubrics. This format ensures all students meet program objectives for accreditation. Course Materials : Required textbooks and resources are offered in a variety of forms, including digital textbooks, digital courseware and physical hard copies. These materials are provided for the faculty free of charge prior to the term beginning. What is expected of me as an online adjunct instructor? Our students are at the center of everything we do. And our online adjunct faculty are essential in ensuring their success. We do this through: Student Support : Provide personalized, 1-on-1 guidance and support to students. Course Feedback : Offer constructive feedback on assignments and course performance every week, for every assignment. There are typically 1-2 assignments that must be graded every week. Grading must be completed within 7 days of when the assignments are due. Timely Responses : Respond to student inquiries within 24 hours. Active Online Presence : Engage in the online classroom consistently throughout the week. This is primarily done through the course discussion board. In most cases, faculty are expected to actively engage in every course discussion. Flexibility : Our students are all around the world. That’s why we ask you to accommodate their diverse backgrounds, experiences, schedules and time zones. Effective Communication : Clearly communicate concepts and foster open dialogue throughout the course. This will include weekly course announcements, discussion board engagement, grading feedback and more. Collaboration : Work with advising and academic support teams to enhance student success. Commitment to Student Success : Strive to help students achieve their academic goals. Professional Development : Learn the latest teaching methods and subject knowledge to ensure academic excellence. How long is an online term at SNHU? SNHU online courses run on a term schedule . There are 6 undergraduate terms per year, lasting 8 weeks each, and 5 graduate terms per year, lasting 10 weeks each. What will be my compensation as an online adjunct? How often will I be paid? Typically, we offer the following standard compensation: $2,200 per 8-week undergraduate course $2,500 per 10-week graduate course Please note that our nursing programs have a separate compensation structure. Undergraduate and graduate adjuncts are paid biweekly and are considered W2 employees. What should I know about SNHU's Hiring Policy? At SNHU, we are committed to creating an inclusive and transparent hiring process. Our Hiring Policy outlines the steps we take to ensure fairness, consistency, and a positive candidate experience from application to onboarding. Whether you’re applying for your first role with us or looking to grow your career here, this policy is designed to support you every step of the way. Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/academics-teaching/": {
      "title": "Academics & Teaching",
      "description": "Academics & Teaching | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Academics & Teaching Adjunct Instructors and full-time professors. Faculty leads and deans. Learning resource specialists and faculty support. Curriculum development and course design. At SNHU, there are countless opportunities to contribute to our mission of student success. Whether you're teaching your favorite subject or designing innovative programs — on campus or online — you'll go above and beyond for some of the most incredible, resilient learners in the world. If this sounds like you, you’re in the right place. Academics & teaching jobs Teach college classes online Looking to make a direct and lasting impact on students from all over the world? As an online instructor at SNHU, you'll do just that. If you're interested in a remote, part-time position with purpose, we've got just the job for you. More about online teaching jobs We're looking for... Motivating mentors Who are enthusiastic about their work — and their students. Optimistic educators Who sincerely believe higher ed is for everyone. Industry pros Who are excited to bring their real-world experience to the classroom. Lifelong learners Who know their stuff, but know they don’t know everything. Our people say it best As an instructor, I encourage my students to come into the classroom and to bring their experiences with them. And those experiences allow us as a unit, as a class, as a whole, to really make transformation possible. Chris M. Campus Faculty Open opportunities Check out the latest roles available in academics and teaching. Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Ethics Save Saved Adjunct Remote See more jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/business-operations-technology/": {
      "title": "Business Operations & Technology",
      "description": "Business Operations & Technology | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Business Operations & Technology With your skills, higher ed may be an unexpected industry. But at SNHU, data-driven strategy and innovative technology have always been at the center of our success. Growing, innovating and leading the industry is what we’re all about. We need people who are determined to make big things happen. To use their skills for good. Who want to solve real problems for real people. Because we’re on a mission to reinvent what college looks like, and we can’t do it without people like you. Business ops and tech jobs We’re looking for… Mission-minded strategists Who collaborate across departments to produce great work. Pragmatic visionaries Who embrace big ideas while understanding scope and capacity. Do-good thinkers Who know the best work happens when you lean into logic and lead with heart. Agile innovators Who are comfortable working outside the box and can think on their feet. Our people say it best We support our partner teams with critical issues that are complex to resolve, or need additional time or that high touch. Lee C. Solutions Team Open opportunities Check out the latest available roles in business operations and technology. Director of Information Security Engineering Save Saved Information Technology Remote Senior Financial Analyst Strategic Initiatives and Technology Advancements Save Saved Finance Remote Custodial Technician I Save Saved Facilities and Operational Services On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/campus-staff/": {
      "title": "Campus Staff",
      "description": "Campus Staff | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Campus Staff When it comes to working on a college campus, it’s about the place and the people. Tucked away in its own corner of Manchester, NH, SNHU campus is a vibrant community connected by good people doing great things. It’s buzzing, exciting and full of energy. It’s 300 acres with nearly 3,000 students. And no matter what role, department or building you work in, you can grow your career while helping students find their place. Campus staff jobs We're looking for... Enthusiastic collaborators Who connect across departments to do what’s best for students. Nimble leaders Who aren’t afraid to shake things up with innovative ideas. Champions of compassion Who see greatness in all students and help them see it, too. New England neighbors Who are motivated by on-site work and connecting face to face. Our people say it best Play video My team is special because we're working with students that have true obstacles. Our goal is to remove them. And they're nonacademic — they're life issues. We're in that mission together. Dan P. Campus Student Wellness Open opportunities Check out the latest available roles for staff on campus. Part-Time Assistant Baseball Coach Save Saved Athletics On-Site (New Hampshire) Campus Public Safety Officer - 3rd Shift Save Saved SNHU and Campus Services On-Site (New Hampshire) Part-time Women's Soccer Club Coach Save Saved Athletics On-Site (New Hampshire) See more jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/customer-service-student-support/": {
      "title": "Customer Service & Student Support",
      "description": "Customer Service & Student Support | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Customer Service & Student Support Student support: it’s what sets us apart as a university. It’s being a friendly voice on the other end of the phone. It’s taking the time to check in — on homework and life at home. It’s helping a first-generation student understand their tuition funding options. It’s sending a handwritten card after finding out they nailed the job interview. As part of the student support team, you’ll see the direct impact you have on students’ lives every single day . If you want to work with students, we want to work with you . Student support jobs Play video The best support in higher ed When you join our customer service and student support staff, it’s no secret you’ll be on the phone (a lot). In this video, our team shares what makes their work feel impactful. Purposeful. Human. And that no matter your role, making a difference will be your new normal. We're looking for... Friendly listeners Who never get tired of getting to know their students — as learners and as people. Trusted guides Who equip students with the tools they need to achieve their goals (and a push to see them through). Proactive problem-solvers Who know which barriers hold students back, and how to remove them before they crop up. Tireless cheerleaders Whose unwavering support gives students the confidence to cross the finish line. Our people say it best I know that I make a difference, and I know that I can transform lives. Nina P. Academic Advising Open opportunities Check out the latest customer service and student support roles at SNHU. Admission Team Lead Save Saved Student Services Remote Admission Processing Coordinator I Save Saved Student Services Hybrid See all jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/human-resources-strategy/": {
      "title": "Human Resources & Strategy",
      "description": "Human Resources & Strategy | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Human Resources & Strategy If you want to make SNHU better for everyone , we’ve got the job for you. From talent acquisition to strategic planning, you can explore opportunities in various roles that help us all succeed. Maybe you’ll be part of the HR People Team, building a culture that truly supports employees in the moments that matter. Or maybe you’ll join the People Experience and Inclusion Team, creating a community where all identities are represented and respected. Or, work with the Strategic Team, mapping a clear path forward for the university and its people. No matter what role you’re in, you’ll provide the support and sense of belonging people need to be their full, authentic selves. Human resources and strategy jobs We're looking for... Active listeners Who will stop at nothing to make sure people feel seen, heard and respected. Proactive changemakers Who are determined to identify opportunities to optimize the employee experience. People-centered strategists Who love to collaborate and problem-solve with leaders and employees. Future-focused innovators Who aren’t afraid to think outside of the box to challenge the status quo. Our people say it best Play video When we think about what this team offers, it’s human skills — our ability to connect, communicate, collaborate, understand and regulate our emotions more effectively. James M. Talent Development Open opportunities Check out the latest available roles in human resources and strategy. University Privacy Officer Save Saved Office of the President Remote See more jobs Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on every team, we share a commitment to our mission — because we believe in education’s power to truly transform lives. More about us Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/career-areas/marketing-communications/": {
      "title": "Marketing & Communications",
      "description": "Marketing & Communications | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Marketing & Communications If you’re worried that working for a university’s marketing team might be boring, we’re kind of offended. You’re reading our work right now (and we had fun writing this). Whether your background is in e-commerce, finance, healthcare or technology, you can use your talents to build a career you’re proud of at SNHU. When you join the marketing and communications team, you can tell stories. Build campaigns. Solve problems. You’ll find yourself among peers who have worked at successful startups and award-winning agencies — people who are eager to share their experience and learn from yours. And best of all? You’ll do good work for a cause you can feel good about. Marketing and communications jobs We're looking for... Honest storytellers Who use real data and talk to real people to paint an authentic picture of SNHU. Tireless troubleshooters Who don’t ask if we can accomplish something, but how we can do it. Captains of creativity Who bring their biggest, boldest ideas aboard. (We’ll only reel you in if you need it.) Marketing wizards Who are magicians of their craft, but always eager to learn new tricks. Our people say it best Play video We get our name out there, and spread awareness, and make potential learners feel like they have a place here at SNHU. Ashley L. Marketing Operations Delivering hope through education No matter what role you step into at Southern New Hampshire University, you’ll have the opportunity to do work that matters. In every department, on 