    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014706/clinical-faculty-global-health-ma-public-health/": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Academics Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health Full time August 26, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is looking for a full-time Clinical Faculty member to support the Global Health concentration within the Master of Public Health program. As a faculty member, reporting to the Director, Program Health, you will teach standardized, predeveloped online graduate level public health courses. You will also contribute to curriculum quality and program support learner success, and help prepare students to address complex public health challenges across national and global contexts. You bring demonstrated expertise in global or international public health and applied public health practice, with experience connecting evidence, equity, culture, health systems, and community priorities to population health action. As a learner-centered educator, you'll connect theory to practice, support diverse adult learners, and contribute to a collaborative academic environment. What You Will Do Teach 30 credit hours annually in standardized, predeveloped online graduate public health courses. Apply instructional practices and strategies that engage adult learners while following approved course design, learning outcomes, and required instructional materials. Conduct appropriate learner outreach and support students who may need additional engagement or clarification of course concepts. Participate in academic review and assessment of MPH Applied Practice Experiences, including review of practicum plans, applied practice products, competency documentation, and development of practice-based or service-learning opportunities. Support identification of practice sites, practice topics, and community engaged learning opportunities in collaboration with program leadership and operational partners. Participate in program events, graduation activities, professional development, and other academic activities that support the MPH program. Apply global health knowledge through case-based learning, current examples, research informed practice, and professional experience. Emphasize ethical, equitable, culturally responsive, and community informed approaches to global public health across diverse populations and settings. Support student understanding of global disease burden, health systems, ethical global partnerships, environmental and social determinants of health, health disparities, and culturally responsive public health practice. What We Are Looking For Doctoral degree in public health or a related discipline from a CEPH accredited school or program, with education and professional experience appropriate to graduate level public health teaching. Demonstrated expertise in global or international public health and applied public health practice. At least three years of professional public health practice experience. At least three years of teaching experience, including experience in an online or technology mediated learning environment. Experience with competency-based education, curriculum assessment, Applied Practice Experiences, Integrative Learning Experiences, internships, capstones, or other graduate public health practice-based learning. Experience with CEPH accreditation, curriculum mapping, program assessment, or accreditation related work. Experience mentoring graduate students, supporting applied practice or capstone projects, or supervising field based public health learning. Experience working with diverse communities, public health organizations, or cross-cultural partners. Additional Qualifications That Would Strengthen Candidacy Master of Public Health or other graduate public health degree from a CEPH accredited school or program. Doctoral concentration, research focus, or substantial professional practice in global health, international health, public health practice, health equity, humanitarian health, or a related area. Experience teaching in an online graduate public health program. Certified in Public Health (CPH) or another relevant professional credential. #LI-Remote This is a remote position. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $70,729.00 - $113,188.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $78,155.00 - $105,739.00. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Healthcare Data Management Save Saved Adjunct Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Ethics Save Saved Adjunct Remote See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014707/applied-practice-experience-administrator-masters-public-health/": {
      "title": "Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health",
      "description": "Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Academics Applied Practice Experience Administrator, Masters Public Health Full time August 26, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far At SNHU, you'll have the option to work remotely in the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Arkansas, Delaware, Florida, Georgia, Hawaii, Idaho, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Mississippi, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Mexico, North Carolina, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming. We ask that our remote employees have access to a reliable internet connection and a dedicated, properly equipped workspace that is free of distractions. Employees must reside in, and work from, one of the above approved states. The opportunity As the Applied Practice Experience Administrator for Masters in Public Health Program, you will serve as a full-time member of Southern New Hampshire University's Global Campus and provides operational administration for the Master of Public Health Applied Practice Experience (APE), referred to within the MPH program as the practicum. You'll support students from preparation through completion and helps ensure consistent, timely, and well documented processes for practice site and preceptor documentation, practicum plan administration, partnership coordination, student progression, quality assurance, and accreditation evidence. Reporting to the Director, Public Health, you'll work with Public Health faculty, Career Services, Academic Advising, Accreditation and Compliance partners, students, preceptors, and practice sites. You will coordinate the operational lifecycle of the APE and maintain records and processes that support applicable Council on Education for Public Health (CEPH) accreditation requirements and university policies. Academic approval of APE plans and assessment of student competency completion remain with designated Public Health faculty or program leadership. What you'll do: Coordinate the operational lifecycle of the MPH Applied Practice Experience from student readiness and planning through completion and required documentation. Be a primary operational liaison among the MPH program, students, preceptors, practice sites, Career Services, academic advising, and other university partners involved in the APE process. Communicate with students regarding APE requirements, timelines, required documentation, and next steps. Coordinate the collection and initial administrative review of preceptor curriculum vitae or résumés, practice site information, and student practicum plans for completeness and established program requirements. Route materials requiring academic judgment, competency review, exceptions, or final academic approval to designated Public Health faculty or program leadership. Maintain accurate practice site, preceptor, affiliation agreement, student progression, and APE completion records across approved university systems. Maintain practice site and preceptor directories and support systematic evaluation of practice sites and the student experience. Maintain relationships with public health, healthcare, governmental, nonprofit, community-based, and other appropriate organizations to expand high-quality APE opportunities. Identify and report current and anticipated APE capacity needs and support short-term and long-term planning for student placements. Coordinate affiliation agreement development, routing, tracking, renewal, and communication in collaboration with appropriate university offices and external partners. Track student progress against APE requirements, identify missing or delayed items, and escalate irregularities or barriers that may affect student progression.· Collect and organize student, preceptor, and practice site feedback and completion data to support quality improvement and program decision-making. Provide reports, key performance indicators, trends, risks, and recommendations to Public Health program leadership. Support program leadership in maintaining documentation and evidence related to CEPH requirements for MPH Applied Practice Experiences and other applicable accreditation expectations. Track required APE documentation, approvals, applied practice products, and completion records in collaboration with designated faculty and program leadership. Support accreditation reporting, self study preparation, evidence requests, and monitoring activities related to the APE. Monitor operational compliance with applicable university requirements, practice site requirements, and approved APE procedures. Quality Assurance and Process Improvement Help develop, documenting, maintaining, and periodically reviewing standard operating procedures for the APE process. Analyze operational data, processing times, student progression, practice site capacity, and partner feedback to identify opportunities to improve student experience and program effectiveness. Support implementation of approved APE workflows and documentation standards across students, faculty reviewers, and university partners. Recommend process improvements that strengthen efficiency, transparency, quality, and accreditation readiness. What we're looking for: Bachelor's degree in public health, healthcare administration, higher education, education, business administration, or a related field. 1+ years of experience in public health, higher education, experiential education, student services, program administration, accreditation, compliance, or a related setting. Manage complex processes, documentation, deadlines, and multiple partners. Demonstrated experience using data to support operational decisions, student success, or quality improvement. Proficiency with Microsoft 365, database systems, and technology platforms used for student support, program management, or experiential education. Preferred Qualifications Master of Public Health or related graduate degree. Knowledge of CEPH accreditation requirements and MPH Applied Practice Experiences. 1+ years of experience coordinating practicums, internships, field education, service learning, or other applied practice activities. Experience working with public health agencies, healthcare organizations, governmental organizations, nonprofit organizations, or community-based partners. Certified in Public Health (CPH), if applicable. Experience with reporting, workflow tools, or experiential learning management platforms. #LI-Remote This is a remote position. We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. Compensation The annual pay range for this position is $48,301.00 - $77,296.00. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. We expect this position to be hired in the following target hiring range $53,373.00 - $72,210.00. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As a full-time employee at SNHU, you’ll get: High-quality, low-deductible medical insurance Low to no-cost dental and vision plans 5 weeks of paid time off (plus almost a dozen paid holidays) Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Parental leave Mental health and wellbeing resources Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Clinical Faculty, Global Health, MA Public Health Save Saved Academics Remote Manager Data Governance Save Saved Information Technology Remote Campus Public Safety Officer - 3rd Shift Save Saved SNHU and Campus Services On-Site (New Hampshire) See all jobs Expect the unexpected As a university, it’s no surprise we employ many talented academics. What you may not know is that SNHU isn’t solely made up of folks with higher ed experience. Not even close. Where will your talent take you? See all teams Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Don't see the job you're looking for? Connect with us anyway! We post new jobs frequently, and joining our talent community is a great way to be notified when we do. Join talent community Sitemap Cookies Corporate site © SNHU 2026, all rights reserved. Thank you, your preferences have been updated. Manage Preferences Accept All Essential Only"
    },
    "https://jobs.snhu.edu/en/jobs/r0014735/online-adjunct-faculty-environmental-ethics/": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Ethics,  | SNHU Careers Skip to main content Who We Are Who We Are Culture Benefits Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Military Career Areas Career Areas Online Teaching Jobs Academics & Teaching Business Operations & Technology Campus Staff Customer Service & Student Support Human Resources & Strategy Marketing & Communications Student Jobs Working at SNHU Working at SNHU Flexible Work Training & Development How We Hire 0 My Saved Jobs Search Jobs Adjunct Online Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Ethics Part time August 25, 2026 Remote Description Southern New Hampshire University is a team of innovators. World changers. Individuals who believe in progress with purpose. Since 1932, our people-centered strategy has defined us — and helped us grow a team that now serves over 180,000 learners worldwide. Our mission to transform lives is made possible by talented people who bring diverse industry experience, backgrounds and skills to the university. And today, we're ready to expand our reach. All we need is you. Make an impact — from near or far We currently have remote adjunct opportunities available in all US States, with the exception of California. The opportunity Southern New Hampshire University is looking for online adjunct faculty within our Undergraduate Liberal Arts program for Global Campus. You will engage students in an asynchronous and inclusive learning environment by providing guidance and resources in a pre-developed online course. You will support students by providing instruction, feedback, and experiential and application-based learning that helps our students achieve their learning and career goals. You will report to the faculty dean team. This is a remote position. What you'll do: Prioritize Student Engagement – Work with students by responding within set timeframes and reaching out proactively to students needing additional support. Recognize student needs holistically and connect them with resources. Encourage participation, collaboration, and strong faculty-student relationships to enhance learning and build skills. Share Expertise and Resources – Stay current in your field of expertise, share your experience, and recommend relevant supplementary materials to enhance student understanding of course content. Find accessible ways to explain complex topics. Offer Feedback & Assessment – Evaluate student work and provide individualized, constructive feedback within set timeframes to promote growth and mastery of course outcomes. Facilitate Discussions – Encourage student interaction through active participation in online discussions while fostering an inclusive, engaging, and respectful environment that promotes open dialogue and diverse perspectives. Courses: PHL-363 Environmental Ethics What we're looking for: A Masters degree in Philosophy, Environmental Science, Natural Resources Management, Environmental Law and Policy, Sustainability, or related field 1+ years of relevant industry experience We believe real innovation comes from inclusion - where different experiences, perspectives and talents are celebrated. So if you're wondering whether SNHU is right for you, take the leap and apply. You might be just the person we're looking for. Compensation The standard compensation for courses is $2,200 per 8-week undergraduate course and $2,500 per 10-week graduate course. Actual pay is determined at the time of course assignment based on discipline. Exceptional benefits (because you’re exceptional) You’re the whole package. Your benefits should be, too. As an employee at SNHU, you'll get: Employer-funded retirement Free tuition program Professional development opportunities Apply Now Save Saved Share Share Related Jobs Online Adjunct Faculty - Computer Science- Full Stack I Development Save Saved Adjunct Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Accounting-Managerial Accounting Save Saved Adjunct Remote Online Adjunct Faculty - Computer Science-Computational Graphics 